Comment: Subset of Noto Sans Symbols2 2.003 to U+25C8, U+25CE and U+2B21
 (pyftsubset, all name IDs and layout features kept), then RENAMED: name
 IDs 1, 4 and 6 read "Seabass Symbols", "Seabass Symbols Regular" and
 "SeabassSymbols-Regular". The rename is load-bearing rather than
 cosmetic. Declared under its upstream family name, this subset and a
 system-installed Noto Sans Symbols2 both answer to "Noto Sans Symbols2",
 and which of them gets painted is not the application's to choose --
 while the catalog glyph's centring is computed from the metrics of the
 other. Regenerating the subset without redoing the rename brings that
 back, on Linux machines with Noto installed only, which is the hardest
 version of it to notice. The OFL notice (name ID 0) and the licence
 URLs (13, 14) are untouched, and ID 3 still records the upstream
 version it was cut from.

